      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {
        "lc_note": {
          "source": "en",
          "texts": {
            "en": {
              "text": "# LC Model Merge (any precision) 🧪\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Where this stands\n- Built 2026-10-10, ModelBuilder 0.4.0 (not pushed yet).\n- Core merge fails with a bf16 model1 and an fp8 model2, and an fp8 model1 rounds the result down to fp8. This node decodes the quantized one first and keeps a **bf16** result, in either order.\n\n**LC Model Merge (any precision)**\n- **ratio**: 0 = all model1, 1 = all model2.\n- **block_ratios**: optional, one value per block (Krea 2 has 28), comma list.\n- **report** shows what each model was stored as and which one became the base.\n\n**This test**\n- Krealism **fp8** + Turbo **bf16** at 0.5. It should look like a normal 50/50 merge (tested within fp8 rounding of the same merge done in pure bf16).\n\n**LC Diffusion Model Save**\n- **enabled** is off. Turn it on to keep the merged model (bf16, about 26 GB).\n\n---"
            }
          },
          "titles": {
            "en": "Read me"
          }
        },
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "English ✏️",
        "# LC Model Merge (any precision) 🧪\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Where this stands\n- Built 2026-10-10, ModelBuilder 0.4.0 (not pushed yet).\n- Core merge fails with a bf16 model1 and an fp8 model2, and an fp8 model1 rounds the result down to fp8. This node decodes the quantized one first and keeps a **bf16** result, in either order.\n\n**LC Model Merge (any precision)**\n- **ratio**: 0 = all model1, 1 = all model2.\n- **block_ratios**: optional, one value per block (Krea 2 has 28), comma list.\n- **report** shows what each model was stored as and which one became the base.\n\n**This test**\n- Krealism **fp8** + Turbo **bf16** at 0.5. It should look like a normal 50/50 merge (tested within fp8 rounding of the same merge done in pure bf16).\n\n**LC Diffusion Model Save**\n- **enabled** is off. Turn it on to keep the merged model (bf16, about 26 GB).\n\n---"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "language": "English ✏️",
        "text": "# LC Model Merge (any precision) 🧪\n\n### 🛑🚫✋ Where this stands\n- Built 2026-10-10, ModelBuilder 0.4.0 (not pushed yet).\n- Core merge fails with a bf16 model1 and an fp8 model2, and an fp8 model1 rounds the result down to fp8. This node decodes the quantized one first and keeps a **bf16** result, in either order.\n\n**LC Model Merge (any precision)**\n- **ratio**: 0 = all model1, 1 = all model2.\n- **block_ratios**: optional, one value per block (Krea 2 has 28), comma list.\n- **report** shows what each model was stored as and which one became the base.\n\n**This test**\n- Krealism **fp8** + Turbo **bf16** at 0.5. It should look like a normal 50/50 merge (tested within fp8 rounding of the same merge done in pure bf16).\n\n**LC Diffusion Model Save**\n- **enabled** is off. Turn it on to keep the merged model (bf16, about 26 GB).\n\n---"
      },
